    # New rows go at the END so M-numbers never shift.
    ("Results", "KEY FINDING: limit-order favorites (parked)", "Posting limit orders on the favorite side (60-97c) made +6.2% per $ in diesel, range +1.4% to +10.4%. First result with a range above zero. Lost in October, gas doesn't confirm, fills not guaranteed. Parked by Dan Nov 26; revisit after the truckstop test.", "seller + favorite", "5,6", "Parked"),
    ("Strategy", "The one direction", "What does the 10 AM crowd miss, and when does it learn it? Order: truckstop scorecard, size the prize, pin mystery moves to a clock. Other fronts paused.", "miss -> when -> why", "6", "Current"),
    ("Results", "Truckstop day 1", "Nov 25: Love's cut about 15% of stores in one batch around 5 PM ET (about -6c each, -1c averaged). TA didn't move. The crowd's forecast didn't react. One day only.", "5 PM batch", "6", "Open"),
    ("System", "Truckstop scorecard", "Scores itself every hour: truckstop move vs what the crowd missed. No large backtest is possible (no free truckstop history). First read at 10 scored days, PASS at 20+.", "ts move vs surprise", "6", "Current"),
    ("System", "Session handoff", "CLAUDE.md section 0 = start/end checklist for every chat; section 6 = the one live direction. One home per fact; write the test before running it.", "read -> work -> log", "6", "Current"),
    ("Gaps", "13 understanding gaps", "Ranked in research/2026-11-26_gaps-and-direction.md. Top 4: is the prize big enough, what window is in AAA's number, how much of AAA is truckstops, who are the informed takers.", "G1-G13", "6", "Open"),
    ("Risk", "Max bet size (first read)", "A $1K bet fills at the shown price (96% of favorite quotes). $5K fits only about half the time and moves the price; $10K rarely fits (17%). Whole market trades about $35K a day; only 3 trades over $5K in 60 days. One afternoon of order book so far; no 10 AM read yet.", "$1K ok / $5K hard / $10K no", "6", "Open"),
    ("Results", "Deep scan: no morning edge", "About 1,980 tests on 114 diesel and 216 gas days. No stored parameter predicts which way the 10 AM crowd is wrong (0 of 38). The all-parameter model makes the forecast worse. Reliable results are losers: cheap long shots (3-25c) lose about 70%; gas YES at 10 AM loses in every band.", "0 of 38", "6", "Current"),
    ("Results", "CANDIDATE: evening crowd overshoots a rise", "After the strongest 5-day rises, buying NO at 9-11 PM (lines 25c and up) made +28% per $ in gas (63 days, range +17% to +39%; last 40% of days +20%). Diesel same sign on 13 days. Found by a follow-up test; can't be tested now because prices are falling. Needs a forward test.", "rising -> NO in the evening", "6", "Open"),
    ("System", "Phone command skill", "One saved skill named kalshi: start, livetest, algo, architecture, save, command. Works in any new chat.", "kalshi + one word", "6", "Current"),
    ("Strategy", "Stage: raw data collection", "Dan, Nov 26: build the biggest clean canvas first (gas + diesel, daily + weekly + monthly, every sub-input), then custom arrays (regimes, Sharpe-style scoring) on top. Replaces the Nov 26 morning pause on gas and weekly/monthly.", "collect -> arrays -> test", "6", "Current"),
    ("Data", "Backtest master", "One table for both fuels and all three time slices: 576 events, 12,845 snapshots (open, 10 AM, noon, 3 PM, 6 PM, 10 PM, close), 155 columns, with the 3 most liquid lines, crowd center, 73 inputs and regime labels. Lives in GitHub data/lake/master; the rulebook is inside tools/backtest_master.py. Matches the old daily panels exactly on 356 shared days.", "fuel x slice x snapshot", "6", "Current"),
    ("Data", "Kalshi historical tier", "Kalshi keeps older markets on a separate historical tier we had never pulled. Gas weekly went from 10 to 139 events (back to Oct 2023), gas monthly 2 to 34. Diesel only began Aug 2026 (116 daily, 16 weekly, 3 monthly), and gas daily did not run in 2025. That is all there is.", "live + historical", "6", "Current"),
    ("Data", "More Kalshi fuel markets found", "Kalshi lists 289 fuel-related series, including 100 state-level daily gas markets and older weekly/monthly gas and diesel tickers. Raw pull queued Nov 26; not yet in the master.", "289 series", "6", "Open"),
    ("Data", "AAA history vetted", "AAA daily is verified back to mid-2024 (diesel) and Sep 2023 (gas). The sample bot's AAA file was dropped: only half its days matched official prints. Still missing: rack prices, station history, natural gas futures.", "verified days only", "6", "Current"),
    ("Verdict", "All 6 markets settle the same way", "All 6 markets settle on the same thing: AAA's national number for ONE date (weekly = Monday, monthly = last day of month), not an average. Checked against outside AAA prints: 530 of 531 events identical. What differs is the design: days open (0.7 / 6.6 / 31), strike step (0.5c / 2c / 5-10c), close time, fees (gas monthly has maker fees), and volume (weekly and monthly trade far more per event).", "same answer, different design", "6", "Current"),
    ("Results", "Crowd prices long markets differently", "The crowd prices long markets differently. Its range grows from about 1c at 1 day to 4-6c at 4-7 days and 10-39c beyond two weeks; its typical miss grows from 0.36c to about 2-4c. It leans on wholesale futures about 6x more at 4-7 days than at 1 day. Description only, not a test.", "longer = wider + more futures", "6", "Open"),
    ("Data", "Old gas weekly was one line", "Before 2026 the weekly gas market was a single yes/no line (95 events) and monthly gas had 6-10 lines. Ladder tests on gas weekly only work from 2026 (45 events).", "era matters", "6", "Current"),
    ("Data", "Inputs Map vs master", "41 of the 83 Inputs Map items are columns in the master, 20 are partly there (mostly live-only since Nov 25), 22 are not collected. Biggest real gap: same-day futures at the noon / 3 PM / 6 PM snapshots. Status per input is in the Inputs Map sheet, column O.", "41 / 20 / 22", "6", "Current"),
    ("System", "Check before building", "New rule in CLAUDE.md and the kalshi skill: read the market's own rules and write its fact card first; every plan lists what is verified and what is assumed.", "verified vs assumed", "6", "Current"),
    ("Results", "Market-maker equation v0 (all 6)", "First market-maker equation on all 6 markets, scored on events it never saw. Center: explains 79% (diesel daily), 71% (gas daily), 68% (diesel weekly), 72% (gas weekly), 29% (gas monthly); diesel monthly has too few events. Daily center is about 0.7x yesterday's AAA move with almost no futures. Width: not cracked (simple time model fails in 5 of 6). Shape: a bell curve misses each line by about 3 price points everywhere, and long shots are priced 2-3 points richer in weekly and monthly.", "center ok, width no, shape close", "6", "Open"),
    ("Results", "Width layer (B) on all 6", "Tried 4 forms for the crowd's range (width). Cracked only for gas weekly: 55% explained on weeks it never saw (error 43% vs 69% with no model). Gas daily is half way (error 47% vs 83%). Diesel daily, diesel weekly and gas monthly fail on later dates, yet all fit fine when eras are mixed (52-67%). So the form is right but its numbers move over time.", "1 of 6 cracked", "6", "Open"),
    ("Results", "How the 6 widths differ", "Range one day out: about 1c in daily and gas weekly, 1.7c gas monthly, 2.4c diesel weekly. A week out: 2c daily, 4.6c gas weekly, 6-7c gas monthly and diesel weekly. Daily ranges barely grow with time (power 0.35); weekly and monthly grow fast (0.6-0.8). Daily ranges are about 2 lines wide, monthly gas only a third of one line, so monthly width is fuzzy to measure.", "daily flat, long ones grow", "6", "Open"),
    ("Results", "Crowd's range is too wide", "In all 6 markets the final AAA number lands inside the crowd's own range more often than a well-sized range would: 78-88% of the time vs 68%. The crowd is less sure than it should be. This is a hint, not a tested trade: costs are not in it.", "78-88% vs 68%", "6", "Open"),
    ("Verdict", "Gas monthly center not solved", "Gas monthly center is still not solved. Three forms (plain, slow pass-through, scale-free) explain only 19-28% on later months, and 38% with eras mixed. Cause: the market itself changed in 2026 (16-44 lines vs 4-11, and expected moves 2.5x larger), so old months do not teach the new ones. Only 29 events. Diesel monthly has 3 events: cannot be fit yet.", "era drift, 29 events", "6", "Open"),
    ("Results", "Anchor engine (big data first)", "New build: the pump-price engine is fit on outside data only (about 1,050 weeks of EIA pump vs wholesale prices since 2006, plus 500-630 days of AAA), then Kalshi sets just 2 dials per market. Center on events never seen: diesel daily 84% (was 76%), diesel weekly 76% (was 66%), gas weekly 68%, gas daily 63% (was 70%), gas monthly 32% (was 28%). Range: gas weekly 59%, gas monthly 40% (was -4%); both daily markets and diesel weekly still fail. Diesel monthly: 3 events, dials borrowed from gas, not proven.", "2 dials, 5 of 6 scored", "6", "Open"),
    ("Verdict", "Copy is not close enough in price yet", "In price terms the copy is still far off: each line is 6-16 price points from the real price, while the bid-ask gap is 2-4 points. Only 4-18% of lines land inside the real bid-ask. It beats a no-model copy (8-26 points) but is not a usable baseline yet. On half-cent ladders a half-cent center miss moves a line about 15 points.", "6-16 pts vs 2-4 spread", "6", "Open"),
    ("Verdict", "Crowd sees something we do not", "At the 8 AM open the daily crowd is already within 0.3-0.4c of the next AAA number. Our best engine is 0.6-0.7c off; plain yesterday's-move momentum is 0.7c. So the crowd holds an input worth about half our miss from the first minute. Finding that input is the shortest path to a baseline copy (north star: unexplained move = missing input).", "0.35c vs 0.65c at open", "6", "Open"),
    ("Verdict", "8 AM input hunt: not found in history", "Backtested 3 suspects that have history against the crowd's opening number (40 diesel + 98 gas days never seen). Miss to the next AAA number: yesterday's move only 0.81c diesel / 0.62c gas; + last 7 moves 0.76 / 0.56; + day of week 0.62 / 0.40; + wholesale 0.44 / 0.46. Crowd: 0.25 / 0.25. None is the missing input. Day of week is real and was missing from our engine.", "best 0.40-0.44c vs crowd 0.25c", "6", "Open"),
    ("Verdict", "Crowd nearly knows the answer by midnight", "By the close the crowd's center explains 98-99% of the next AAA move (miss 0.12-0.13c), hours before AAA posts at about 3:20 AM. Its miss shrinks through the day, mostly between noon and 6 PM. That is the footprint of a live station-price feed (GasBuddy or OPIS type) that runs ahead of AAA. It has no free history, so it cannot be backtested with data we hold today.", "98-99% by close", "6", "Open"),
    ("Data", "Futures pull was monthly, now fixed + curve", "Found while checking: the full-history futures files held one bar per MONTH, not per day (Yahoo shrinks them when asked for max range). Fixed to real daily bars. Also added the next 4 contract months of gas and diesel futures (the curve), needed for monthly ladders. The master was not hurt: it reads futures from EIA and the project databases.", "daily bars + 4 months out", "6", "Open"),
    ("Data", "Slice table + ratio layer built", "New layers on top of the master, all 6 markets: 23,757 rows (market x event x time x busy line) over 542 events, each with the favorite side (priced above 50%), cost with fee, outcome label (favorite won as Yes / won as No / lost as Yes / lost as No), return per $ for favorite and underdog, plus 11 of our own ratios and 4 labels. File: data/lake/master/slices.csv.gz. Tool: tools/slice_scan.py.", "23,757 rows, 11 ratios", "6", "Open"),
    ("Results", "Underdogs lose everywhere", "Backing the underdog on the busy lines loses 33% to 58% per $ after costs in all 6 markets, in both the early and late blocks. Long shots are overpriced. Favorites win 76-90% of the time but, after costs, only about break even overall (diesel +4%, gas about 0).", "dogs -33% to -58% per $", "6", "Open"),
